.TH ELYTERMINAL 1
.SH NAME
elyterminal \- terminal on GPUI and Ely
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B elyterminal
.RI [ folder ]
.br
.B elyterminal
.BI --working-directory " folder"
.br
.B elyterminal
.BI -d " folder"
.br
.B elyterminal
.BI --startingDirectory " folder"
.SH DESCRIPTION
ELYTerminal is a graphical terminal for X11 and Wayland.
Sessions sit on the left, the terminal in the middle, and Git or Files on the right.
Open Settings with Ctrl-comma to change appearance, shell and terminal settings.
Settings lists the keyboard shortcuts available on the current platform.
Given a folder, the first session starts there.
The directory options accept the forms used by Linux xdg-terminal-exec and
Windows Terminal.
.SH FILES
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ELYTerminal/settings.json
.br
Settings are saved here, or in
.I ~/.config/ELYTerminal/settings.json
when XDG_CONFIG_HOME is unset.
Installing, upgrading or removing a package does not remove this file.
.SH SEE ALSO
.UR https://github.com/ELY-Open-Source/ELYTerminal
ELYTerminal documentation and releases
.UE
